Episode 11

24
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:04,050
Episode 11

25
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:04,050
The Misanthrope and the Nigh Past

26
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:04,050
The Misanthrope and the Nigh Past

27
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:05,980
Social Studies Prep Room

28
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:05,990
Excuse me.

29
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:10,160
Mr. Hitoma, are you here?

30
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,010
I've brought the notebooks 
for world history.

31
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:14,680
Oh, thanks.

32
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:17,540
Wait, huh? Haruna?

33
00:02:18,130 --> 00:02:20,320
Yeah, Mirai Haruna.

34
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:23,280
Still don't remember my name?

35
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,890
No, I remember

36
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:29,220
That's not it. Wasn't Akazawa 
on class duty today?

37
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:32,740
Rio had to go somewhere after school.

38
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,190
I'm filling in for her.

39
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:38,420
Didn't something similar happen before?

40
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:43,060
You mean the time with the committee? 
Or the group assignment?

41
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:45,390
That's way too many times.

42
00:02:46,870 --> 00:02:49,910
Still, I kind of like it 
when people ask me for help.

43
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:55,000
Haruna, you can be strange sometimes.

44
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:58,600
That's not true.

45
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:01,900
Homework for you.

46
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:02,550
What?

47
00:03:03,050 --> 00:03:06,010
Have someone help you out by next week.

48
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:09,690
Do I need to do it, or else?

49
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:10,980
No, not at all.

50
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:11,850
Huh?

51
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:15,230
It's just that I worry a little about you.

52
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:18,060
Feel free to ignore the deadline, too.

53
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,620
You're a weird teacher.

54
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:24,270
Do you mean that like when they say, 
"You're a funny girl?"

55
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:25,150
Huh?

56
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,290
I'm sorry.

57
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:33,540
If I really had a problem, 
I think you're the last one I'd go to.

58
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:35,530
That's fine by me.

59
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,530
As a teacher, it's not like 
I'll always be around for you.

60
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:41,000
How irresponsible.

61
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,500
What do you want? 
That's just how it works.

62
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:51,670
That's why I want you to learn all 
the tricks to living life all by yourself.

63
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,390
I'll be just fine by myself.

64
00:03:54,830 --> 00:03:57,040
That's what everyone thinks at first.

65
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:01,660
So you used to think that way, too?

66
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:02,580
Nope.

67
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:06,320
I quickly gave up on that 
to depend on others all the time.

68
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,940
Life's easy when other people help you.

69
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:13,660
And they get to feel good about it, 
so it's a win-win situation.

70
00:04:14,060 --> 00:04:14,920
Isn't it great?

71
00:04:15,450 --> 00:04:16,970
You're a weird teacher.

72
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:24,320
Rio, good morning!

73
00:04:26,710 --> 00:04:29,170
Good morning, Mirai!

74
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:34,310
I gave the world history notebooks 
to Mr. Hitoma yesterday.

75
00:04:34,310 --> 00:04:37,770
Oh, thanks! You're the best!

76
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,760
No, it's fine.

77
00:04:40,150 --> 00:04:41,900
Anything for you, Rio.

78
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:43,300
Oh, yeah.

79
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:46,110
Can you do one more thing 
for me while you're at it?

80
00:04:46,110 --> 00:04:47,820
Yeah, sure.

81
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:49,400
Awesome!

82
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,470
Love you, Mirai!

83
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:58,120
Social Studies Prep Room

84
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:58,120
Mr. Hitoma, are you what 
people call an otaku?

85
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:03,210
Well, strictly speaking, 
I wouldn't say that exactly,

86
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:06,640
but under a more general 
definition of "otaku"...

87
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:10,170
I suppose that might not be 
an entirely untrue statement...

88
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:11,990
So, which is it?

89
00:05:12,630 --> 00:05:15,260
Sorry. I'm an otaku.

90
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:16,430
Gross.

91
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:18,480
Don't say that 
after taking the time to ask!

92
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,930
I'm kidding.

93
00:05:20,930 --> 00:05:24,060
You're not <i>that</i> gross, Mr. Hitoma.

94
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:26,920
Does that mean I am a little bit?

95
00:05:28,270 --> 00:05:29,650
Kind of?

96
00:05:29,650 --> 00:05:31,580
Oh, forget I asked.

97
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,470
Anyway, Haruna.

98
00:05:33,470 --> 00:05:36,220
You filled in this class 
journal, didn't you?

99
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:42,060
The name says Rio Akazawa, 
but this is your handwriting.

100
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:45,640
Wow, Rio's handwriting 
looks just like mine!

101
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:48,190
This is your writing style as well.

102
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:51,530
Wait, you can tell the difference?

103
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,020
I'm not that stupid, you know.

104
00:05:54,490 --> 00:05:56,240
Did she make you do this again?

105
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:59,270
She just asked me for a favor.

106
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:02,830
Well, keep it to a minimum.

107
00:06:03,690 --> 00:06:05,530
It doesn't do Akazawa any good.

108
00:06:06,970 --> 00:06:08,890
Okay, class is about to start.

109
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:10,400
Get going.

110
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,590
Sure.

111
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:21,450
Hey, Mirai, are you friendly with Hitoma?

112
00:06:21,450 --> 00:06:24,200
Not particularly. Why?

113
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,830
You're always off to 
the social studies prep room.

114
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:29,860
They have books that aren't 
at the school library.

115
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:33,070
Except Mr. Hitoma's there to annoy you.

116
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,540
Do you have a thing for Hitoma?

117
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:37,120
Ugh, no!

118
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:39,790
I know, Mirai.

119
00:06:39,790 --> 00:06:42,990
Wanna skip our next 
history class together?

120
00:06:42,990 --> 00:06:44,050
What?

121
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:46,480
By pretending to go to the nurse.

122
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,940
I don't know about that...

123
00:06:50,590 --> 00:06:52,650
Even if I ask as a favor?

124
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,820
It's bad to ditch class...

125
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:58,030
You wanna listen to Hitoma's lecture?

126
00:06:58,030 --> 00:06:58,820
What?

127
00:07:00,410 --> 00:07:01,240
So boring.

128
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:06,160
Being with you is boring now, Mirai.

129
00:07:11,460 --> 00:07:12,920
Social Studies Prep Room

130
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:19,220
School is kind of like jail.

131
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:21,560
That's a wild comparison.

132
00:07:22,090 --> 00:07:24,690
A place where people 
who just happen to be similar ages

133
00:07:24,690 --> 00:07:29,160
gather at a predetermined time to be 
educated for a predetermined period.

134
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:34,500
And sometimes they make you 
participate in groups.

135
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,960
You don't like doing group work?

136
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:39,420
I'd say that most people don't.

137
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,700
Guess you're right.

138
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,370
Not gonna tell me off?

139
00:07:45,370 --> 00:07:46,160
For what?

140
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:48,830
I mean, I should be in class now.

141
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:51,080
We've got an escaped prisoner here.

142
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:53,900
You're the only one who'd joke like that.

143
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,130
Maybe so.

144
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:57,270
So? Not gonna yell at me?

145
00:07:57,270 --> 00:07:59,340
I've been here every day lately.

146
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:02,190
It's fine if sometimes, 
you just don't feel like it.

147
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:04,730
And this is a free period for me.

148
00:08:04,730 --> 00:08:06,740
That makes you my partner in crime.

149
00:08:06,740 --> 00:08:11,100
Nuh-uh! I'm preparing for my next class!

150
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:13,060
What's that?

151
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:15,820
Kind of like lesson prep 
and a cheat sheet in one.

152
00:08:40,660 --> 00:08:42,270
Hey, Mr. Hitoma.

153
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:44,810
What would you do if the 
world was going to end?

154
00:08:45,150 --> 00:08:46,370
Where'd that come from?

155
00:08:46,370 --> 00:08:48,630
Just a what-if.

156
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:50,750
Let me think.

157
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,610
I'd beat all the games 
I never got around to.

158
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:56,100
Seriously?

159
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:58,610
It's important to me.

160
00:08:58,610 --> 00:09:00,660
Even with the world ending?

161
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:04,950
Wouldn't you normally choose to spend it 
with your girlfriend or your family?

162
00:09:05,590 --> 00:09:07,070
Is that what you'd pick, Haruna?

163
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:13,170
I think... I would lie.

164
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:14,340
Lie?

165
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:15,180
Yeah.

166
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:19,410
I'd lie and say, "There's no way 
the world's going to end."

167
00:09:19,410 --> 00:09:24,910
And I'd spend my last moments living 
normally with the people who believed me.

168
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,520
How kind of you.

169
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,420
Huh?

170
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:32,430
I mean, aren't you lying for those 
who can't accept that it's all ending?

171
00:09:33,230 --> 00:09:35,390
I'm just dragging them along with me.

172
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:38,980
Since I'm the one who can't accept it.

173
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:43,780
I wish the world would end tomorrow...

174
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:51,990
If you told me, "There's no way 
the world's going to end,"

175
00:09:52,650 --> 00:09:54,670
I think that I'd believe you.

176
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:55,580
What?

177
00:09:55,580 --> 00:09:58,000
But then you can't play video games.

178
00:09:58,340 --> 00:09:59,790
I guess not.

179
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:01,590
It's fine, though.

180
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:04,040
What's <i>that</i> mean?

181
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:07,550
I wasn't trying to drag you 
into it, Mr. Hitoma.

182
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:11,520
So you don't have to believe me.

183
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,730
I don't care if you fool me.

184
00:10:16,570 --> 00:10:20,340
It's fine if you lie, 
so tell me what's on your mind.

185
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:26,060
I'm on your side, Haruna.

186
00:10:29,510 --> 00:10:31,370
Hey...

187
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:36,830
Is it okay... for me to stay here?

188
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:38,650
Yeah.

189
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:50,940
Like I said, Mr. Hitoma...

190
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:54,100
Let's be adults about this.

191
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:57,370
And by adults, you mean?

192
00:10:57,370 --> 00:11:00,960
Teaching's a business, too.

193
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:06,220
Do you understand your obligations 
as an employee of this school?

194
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:11,760
And you know how much the Akazawa 
family contributes in donations.

195
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:13,200
Well, yes.

196
00:11:13,470 --> 00:11:14,810
In that case...

197
00:11:14,810 --> 00:11:18,440
You know what the right 
move is, don't you?

198
00:11:19,770 --> 00:11:21,670
Pretend the bullying didn't happen?

199
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:26,120
Oh, you make me sound 
like the bad guy.

200
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:29,400
There's no proof 
that Akazawa did it, is there?

201
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,630
It'd be nothing but a losing fight.

202
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:36,430
So think about whose side you 
should take for your benefit.

203
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,200
My benefit?

204
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,820
You've got a long life ahead.

205
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:43,090
Think about your career.

206
00:11:43,090 --> 00:11:46,590
You're a bright man, Mr. Hitoma.

207
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:50,110
You'll make the smart decision, won't you?

208
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:54,490
I can't do it.

209
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:58,700
I can't stay quiet about it.

210
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:01,180
I made a promise to Haruna.

211
00:12:01,550 --> 00:12:04,060
I'll be her ally to the end.

212
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:08,280
Mr. Hitoma.

213
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:14,680
Being someone's ally 
also means making enemies.

214
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:15,950
I'm well aware.

215
00:12:18,990 --> 00:12:20,410
Hold on.

216
00:12:20,410 --> 00:12:23,710
Are you in <i>that</i> kind of 
relationship with Haruna?

217
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:24,750
Huh?!

218
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:29,300
I hear Haruna visits the social 
studies prep room quite often.

219
00:12:29,770 --> 00:12:32,460
What's she's been getting up to?

220
00:12:32,790 --> 00:12:34,920
I've just been giving her advice.

221
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:38,470
Say what you will about me, 
but don't insult Haruna like that.

222
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,520
Sure, fine.

223
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:46,460
You've made your intentions 
<i>very</i> clear, Mr. Hitoma.

224
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:49,480
Ill-advised as they may be.

225
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:53,320
It's too bad, Mr. Hitoma.

226
00:12:54,450 --> 00:12:59,660
Principal's Office

227
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,570
Mr. Hitoma.

228
00:12:56,570 --> 00:12:59,660
Surely you know why I've called you here.

229
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:03,260
No. What is it, Vice Principal?

230
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:06,250
That's enough playing dumb.

231
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:10,950
It seems you've been physically 
disciplining Mirai Haruna.

232
00:13:11,550 --> 00:13:12,240
What?

233
00:13:12,460 --> 00:13:15,690
Haruna's been covered 
in fresh bruises lately,

234
00:13:15,690 --> 00:13:18,100
and there are records of her being 
treated in the nurse's office.

235
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:22,470
They must have been 
from your corporal punishment.

236
00:13:22,470 --> 00:13:25,310
You're wrong! I've done 
nothing of the sort!

237
00:13:25,310 --> 00:13:27,620
We have testimony on hand.

238
00:13:27,620 --> 00:13:32,280
You were physically abusing her 
in the social studies prep room.

239
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:33,210
What?

240
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:37,820
And to retaliate, 
Haruna was bullying Akazawa.

241
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:39,820
You're mistaken!

242
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:41,490
Haruna was the one being bulliedâ€”

243
00:13:41,490 --> 00:13:43,280
There's no point making excuses!

244
00:13:43,590 --> 00:13:46,330
Haruna and Akazawa told us all about it!

245
00:13:46,650 --> 00:13:49,130
What? Haruna did?

246
00:13:49,910 --> 00:13:52,740
You will be suspended 
for the foreseeable future.

247
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:56,080
You are not to make contact 
with Haruna or Akazawa.

248
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,030
Is that understood?'

249
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:05,800
<i>Haruna was expelled from school 
for disorderly conduct.</i>

250
00:14:06,270 --> 00:14:10,830
<i>I was forced into resigning as a teacher.</i>

251
00:14:20,430 --> 00:14:21,370
Haruna.

252
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:24,150
So you were here.

253
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,440
It's been a while.

254
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:32,110
Um... are you doing well?

255
00:14:32,710 --> 00:14:36,300
Oh, are you eating properly?

256
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,760
Getting sleep?

257
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:39,700
Just kidding.

258
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:42,750
I pull a lot of all-nighters, 
so I can't speak...

259
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,640
Shut up...

260
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:54,070
Didn't you say you'd 
believe me, even if I lied?

261
00:14:57,060 --> 00:15:00,410
This is all your fault.

262
00:15:04,430 --> 00:15:08,830
I'm the one who lied 
about the physical abuse.

263
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:16,540
You were being a real hassle...

264
00:15:18,490 --> 00:15:21,370
So I figured I'd drag you into it...

265
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:29,630
But you... still believed 
my lies, didn't you?

266
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:35,240
Is this because I tried to step in?

267
00:15:35,980 --> 00:15:38,550
That's right! It's all...

268
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:45,770
your fault for taking my complaints 
seriously and trying to do the impossible!

269
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,370
It's my fault.

270
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:54,580
It's my fault that you...

271
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:56,860
That's right.

272
00:15:58,100 --> 00:15:59,600
That's why, Mr. Hitoma...

273
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:02,800
You got what you deserved.

274
00:16:04,250 --> 00:16:07,620
It's all my fault.

275
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:18,440
Oh, crap!

276
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,950
I'm gonna be late!

277
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,900
Morning, Mr. Hitoma...

278
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,160
Good morning, Ms. Karasuma.

279
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:34,420
Wow, you're pale as a ghost.

280
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:37,100
I'm a little sleep-deprived...

281
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:40,540
Wanna rest in my office 
until the all-school morning assembly?

282
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:43,070
Maybe I will...

283
00:16:43,070 --> 00:16:45,970
Wow! These bottles are so cute!

284
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:49,530
These bottles are unique to our school.

285
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:57,260
Oh, good morning, Haruka, Mr. Hitoma.

286
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:00,440
Mr. Hitoma?

287
00:17:00,870 --> 00:17:02,940
Good morning, Yuki.

288
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:06,170
Is she the new teacher?

289
00:17:06,170 --> 00:17:07,030
Yes!

290
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:12,120
She's our brand new hire, who just 
graduated from a women's college in Tokyo.

291
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:13,590
Nice to meet you.

292
00:17:13,590 --> 00:17:16,180
I'm the brand new hire, Mirai Haruna.

293
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:21,180
I hope to learn a lot 
from you working together!

294
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:22,310
Hey there.

295
00:17:22,310 --> 00:17:25,330
I'm Haruka Karasuma, the school nurse.

296
00:17:25,330 --> 00:17:26,720
And this is...

297
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:29,610
It's been ages, Mr. Hitoma.

298
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:35,650
Mr. Hitoma, Ms. Haruna. 
Do you two know each other?

299
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:38,110
Huh? Well...

300
00:17:38,110 --> 00:17:41,120
Yes, actually, we do!

301
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:44,490
Mr. Hitoma was my homeroom 
teacher back in high school.

302
00:17:45,770 --> 00:17:48,730
And now you're teaching 
at the same school?

303
00:17:48,730 --> 00:17:50,920
As homeroom and assistant 
homeroom teacher!

304
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,950
It must be fate!

305
00:17:52,950 --> 00:17:54,670
Fate?

306
00:17:55,310 --> 00:17:57,680
It's basically the same for you, Yuki.

307
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:02,520
You went after Satoru, your homeroom 
teacher, and ended up at the same school.

308
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:04,490
Is that story true?

309
00:18:04,490 --> 00:18:05,840
Now I'm curious!

310
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:07,640
I'd love to hear all about it!

311
00:18:07,930 --> 00:18:09,140
What?!

312
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:34,660
It's finally your first day. 
Think you'll be all right?

313
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:35,660
Yes!

314
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:38,380
I was surprised at first when 
I learned the truth about this school,

315
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:39,920
but I'm totally fine now.

316
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:43,740
I'm sure there's plenty more 
to surprise you,

317
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:46,880
but you'll be okay with Mr. Hitoma here.

318
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:47,580
What?

319
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:48,510
Yes!

320
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:51,550
I'll have Mr. Hitoma show me the ropes!

321
00:18:51,550 --> 00:18:54,770
Break a leg, Ms. Haruna!

322
00:18:54,770 --> 00:18:56,640
Thank you very much!

323
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:01,940
My first class... I'm nervous.

324
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:05,100
Well, the first day's only introductions.

325
00:19:05,530 --> 00:19:07,900
Don't stress so much, and take it easy.

326
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:12,400
Were you nervous on your 
first day, Mr. Hitoma?

327
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,320
Ah...

328
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:15,500
I totally forgot how it went.

329
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:17,150
Wow.

330
00:19:17,150 --> 00:19:19,590
So you really <i>were</i> able to take it easy.

331
00:19:19,590 --> 00:19:20,360
Nope.

332
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,210
I was so nervous, 
I can't remember any of it.

333
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:28,420
Haruna.

334
00:19:31,470 --> 00:19:34,600
I'm really sorry about back then.

335
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:43,710
You were in a tough situation, 
and I made it worse by stepping in.

336
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:46,250
Mr. Hitoma.

337
00:19:46,820 --> 00:19:48,190
It's all right.

338
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:52,370
I was young back then.

339
00:19:52,670 --> 00:19:53,720
Haruna...

340
00:19:54,410 --> 00:19:57,080
So it's not your fault.

341
00:19:57,600 --> 00:20:00,350
Why don't we forget about that?

342
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:04,180
We're both adults now. Okay?

343
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:07,130
If you say so, Haruna.

344
00:20:07,130 --> 00:20:10,240
What's done is done, 
so let's put it behind us.

345
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,840
Let's work hard together 
as colleagues from now on!

346
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:20,660
I look forward to working 
with you, Ms. Haruna.

347
00:20:21,230 --> 00:20:23,660
I do, too, Mr. Hitoma.

348
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:30,310
Advanced Class

349
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:28,310
This is the advanced class, 
which we're in charge of.

350
00:20:28,650 --> 00:20:29,900
We have six students.

351
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:33,530
Two of them are new faces 
who just moved up this year.

352
00:20:35,060 --> 00:20:36,790
I said, don't be nervous.

353
00:20:37,270 --> 00:20:39,250
Things will go the way they do.

354
00:20:39,250 --> 00:20:40,550
Yes!

355
00:20:40,550 --> 00:20:41,960
Okay, here we go.

356
00:20:47,210 --> 00:20:48,920
Prince Waka!

357
00:20:49,550 --> 00:20:51,920
Look this way!

358
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:55,130
Shoot me in the heart!

359
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:59,140
Thanks for winking at us!

360
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:00,890
Oh, Mr. Rei!

361
00:21:00,890 --> 00:21:03,030
It's great to finally see you again!

362
00:21:03,030 --> 00:21:04,770
I love you today, too!

363
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:08,670
What exactly... is going on here?

364
00:21:08,670 --> 00:21:11,420
This is a makeshift fashion show runway.

365
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:13,860
Would you care to join me, Hitoma?

366
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:15,200
Hitoma?

367
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:17,720
Don't climb up on the desks!

368
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:21,700
And let's address the teachers properly.

369
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:26,890
I do apologize if my actions offended you.

370
00:21:27,210 --> 00:21:31,820
That being said, there's only one 
person I want to address with a title.

371
00:21:36,350 --> 00:21:38,060
You're blushing!

372
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:40,490
Not used to this kinda stuff?

373
00:21:40,490 --> 00:21:43,320
This new teacher seems like a pushover!

374
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:46,480
She looks like a child, 
and even less reliable than Hitoma.

375
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:53,710
But she just screams "new teacher," 
which I find adorable.

376
00:21:54,170 --> 00:21:57,780
There really <i>was</i> plenty more 
to surprise me.

377
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:01,770
Looks like it's gonna 
be another tough year.

378
00:23:33,060 --> 00:23:40,040
Next Episode:

379
00:23:33,060 --> 00:23:40,040
The Misanthrope and Falsehood Found Nigh

